From b989480d424a87a2031e28f9f8532648808ea86a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:37:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: drag to walk, tap to talk, touch on the field menu

Touch for the desktop build (and later the phone builds) beyond the arena's
own screens:

- Drags (native/touch.h, native_touch.c): a press that moves
  TOUCH_DRAG_START (8) pixels is a drag and is never a tap. Touch_Drag gives
  its heading and distance from a centre that trails the finger by at most
  TOUCH_DRAG_REACH (40): a virtual stick wherever the finger went down.
- The field (include/arena/field_touch.h): a drag steers the leader in any
  direction (FIELD_TOUCH_STEER in Actor_UpdatePlayerControl, the drag's
  heading in place of the pad's), and past TOUCH_DRAG_RUN (28) runs; a tap
  in the 96-pixel square round the middle of the safe area, where the camera
  keeps the leader, presses A (talk, check: Field_CheckConfiguredKeys).
- Messages: a tap anywhere moves one on (Text_CheckTextDismissed), and a
  finger held down hurries its text and pauses as a held button does.
- The field menu (include/arena/menu_touch.h): the party row of the
  Psynergy, Item and Status screens and the Psynergy target picker, the
  Psynergy and item lists, and the item commands take taps: a tap selects,
  a tap on the selection presses A, as on every other menu.
- The battle Summon list takes taps and has the lists' Back button
  (BattleTouch_List, BattleTouch_OpenBack), as the Psynergy, Djinn and item
  lists do.
- The headless build's `drag X0 Y0 X1 Y1 N` script command.

Keys and the pad work as before. The GBA ROM has none of it: the hooks are
empty macros there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
